{"id":52323,"ord":111,"n_segments":181,"prev":52322,"next":52324,"doc":{"id":"67256","title":"67256_Paul L. Howard oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Paul L. Howard","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/67256/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=67256"},"chapter":"First years in Los Angeles","title":"Personnel of the Original Creole Orchestra","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Collette reads the band's members from an article; Howard recognises Dink Johnson, Bill Johnson and Baquet.","period":"1915","year_from":1915,"year_to":1915,"words":251,"start":[184,11],"end":[186,10],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=67256#s52323","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Original Creole Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":null}]},"people":[{"name":"George Baquet","qid":"Q362355","n":4},{"name":"Bill Johnson","qid":null,"n":3},{"name":"Paul L. Howard","qid":"Q7151403","n":2},{"name":"Freddie Keppard","qid":"Q490080","n":2},{"name":"Bud Scott","qid":"Q1000534","n":2},{"name":"Dink Johnson","qid":"Q1226517","n":1},{"name":"Dink New Orleans Jimmy","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Eddie Vinson","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Pete Johnson","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":184,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Could you give this for information? Do you need notes? People who (inaudible) in that band? Do you remember any of the names?"},{"p":184,"b":12,"s":"","x":"Any of those that"},{"p":184,"b":13,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Huh?"},{"p":184,"b":14,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Do you remember any of the names? With the band, (inaudible)?"},{"p":184,"b":15,"s":"","x":"Mr. Howard? Started out?"},{"p":184,"b":16,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"No, I don't remember the band."},{"p":184,"b":17,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Did they have a clarinet player?"},{"p":184,"b":18,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yeah, they had a clarinet player. I can't think of that fellow's name."},{"p":185,"b":0,"s":"","x":"HEMLOCK ERASABLE"},{"p":185,"b":1,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Yeah, okay."},{"p":185,"b":2,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Uh--"},{"p":185,"b":3,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Got a sexy name? section there?"},{"p":185,"b":4,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Yeah, (inaudible) right here. this paragraph"},{"p":185,"b":5,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"I can't think of that fellow's name."},{"p":185,"b":6,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Paul remembered them well, and recited the names of the men in the band, but Scott, Bud guitar? retired?"},{"p":185,"b":7,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yep."},{"p":185,"b":8,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"(Reading) The guitar preceded the banjo in (inaudible) the band (inaudible) history, violin? or jazz fiddle. Dink New Orleans Jimmy (inaudible) Pete Johnson, drums. Oh yeah, Dink Johnson? Sure, everybody knows him. Who Pete"},{"p":185,"b":9,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yep, I know him."},{"p":185,"b":10,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"(inaudible)"},{"p":185,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Bill Johnson, bass."},{"p":185,"b":12,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Bill Johnson as bass. in"},{"p":185,"b":13,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Brother?"},{"p":185,"b":14,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"No, he ain't no brother. He just a member of the band."},{"p":185,"b":15,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"He and Bill Johnson were brothers- in-law? How about that? of Jelly Roll Morton?"},{"p":185,"b":16,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"(inaudible) How about that."},{"p":185,"b":17,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Or George McQuay, (unintelligible) clarinet? [Baquet] McQuay"},{"p":185,"b":18,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"George McQuay? (phonetic)."},{"p":185,"b":19,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Yeah."},{"p":186,"b":0,"s":"","x":"HEMLOCK FRAGILE COTTON CONTENT"},{"p":186,"b":1,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"That name doesn't sound familiar at all."},{"p":186,"b":2,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"(inaudible) What do you think that is?"},{"p":186,"b":3,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Well, (inaudible) Baguet. it might be Baguet."},{"p":186,"b":4,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Baguet! Oh, yeah! That's right. Clarinet."},{"p":186,"b":5,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"(inaudible) Eddie Vinson, (phonetic), (inaudible) trombone."},{"p":186,"b":6,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yep."},{"p":186,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"And Tipperd (phonetic) --"},{"p":186,"b":8,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Toppert Keppard"},{"p":186,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Yeah, was on trumpet."},{"p":186,"b":10,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"That's right."}]}